%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 146b4dedcb9af3b4ab5fe5794271c3d8, type: 3}
  m_Name: Ticket_Coc3_Duplicate_Ip
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::TicketData
  ticketId: ticket_coc3_duplicate_ip
  targetModule: 2
  sceneName: COC3-Copy
  title: New PC knocked the office offline
  description: A replacement PC was set up this morning. Since then that machine
    has no network at all, and staff say another computer keeps dropping out too.
  icon: {fileID: 0}
  briefingDialog: {fileID: 0}
  requiredTaskId: ticket_coc3_duplicate_ip
  requiresDiagnosis: 1
  symptomText: The workstation's IP settings look correct and match the documentation.
    No network traffic works. Windows has reported an IP address conflict.
  diagnosisOptions:
  - label: Two devices are using the same IP address
    isCorrect: 1
    feedback: Correct. Everything looks right on both machines, which is what makes
      this one hard - the settings are only wrong in relation to each other. Give
      one of them a different address.
  - label: Faulty network card in the new PC
    isCorrect: 0
    feedback: A dead card would not produce a conflict warning - Windows can only
      report a conflict because the card is working and talking.
  - label: Incorrect default gateway
    isCorrect: 0
    feedback: A wrong gateway breaks traffic to other networks but leaves the local
      network working. Here nothing works at all.
  - label: The switch has failed
    isCorrect: 0
    feedback: A failed switch would take out far more than two machines, and would
      not cause a conflict warning.
